@format 1
@id media-loading.in-edit-tab
@title In Edit tab
@section Media loading
@area In Edit tab
@entry edit-path-change, edit-items-add, edit-media-change
@summary Show Edit-specific selected-path loading, new-item persistent-plan writes, mpv eligibility, and synchronous restoration against the viewer state that exists at publication time.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-loading.common.files-selection, media-loading.common.viewer-gate, media-loading.common.media-publication, media-loading.common.mpv-preview
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag edit

@alias edit = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PEditTab
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[edit-path-change] Edit Files current-path event <input>
= PListPathChange synchronously delivered the current path to PEditPathShow.
> edit-path-result

[edit-items-add] Edit newly-added-items event <input>
= PListItemsAdd synchronously delivered all newly added entries after the first-new-path selection handler returned.
> edit-items-result

[edit-media-change] Edit viewer-media event <input>
= PViewerMediaRaise reached Edit's PViewerMediaChange subscriber during the common publication call.
> edit-restore

[edit-path-result] Edit selected-path adapter <decision>
- Log the selected file/persistence state, ignore blank selection, and request a nonblank source from the Edit viewer @ edit.PEditPathShow(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerEditEligible
! The Edit viewer is constructed with PViewerEditEligible=true; current non-Edit media-tab viewers leave it false, so only Edit can make Common / Viewer gate select configured mpv.
? "Nonblank current path" > map:media-loading.common.viewer-gate
? "Blank current path" > edit-no-request

[edit-items-result] Carried Edit plan available <decision>
- PEditItemsHandle returns while plan loading is active or when no carried persistent Edit plan exists @ edit.PEditItemsHandle(...)
? "Carried plan applies" > edit-items-save
? "No carried plan" > edit-items-nochange

[edit-restore] Edit state restoration during publication <process>
- PEditCropRestore does not use the LCargo passed to the event; it restores source-specific and carried crop/edit state from the viewer's current PViewerSourcePath and crop state at the moment this subscriber runs @ edit.PEditCropRestore(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerSourcePath
! Successful Flyleaf/mpv commits assign PViewerSourcePath before PViewerMediaRaise, so restoration then targets the newly committed source before those commit methods continue into preview restoration, autoplay/pause, and final playback-state updates.
! Backend load failure is different: PViewerLoadHandle raises a failure cargo without replacing PViewerSourcePath, so Edit restores against the previously committed source, if any. Viewer close clears PViewerSourcePath before publishing its empty cargo.
> edit-restored

[edit-no-request] Edit viewer request omitted <output>
= Edit logs the empty selection and does not call the shared viewer-loading pipeline.

[edit-items-save] Save carried Edit plan for each new entry <process>
- For every added entry, read any source-specific Edit plan, resolve it against the carried plan, and save the resolved result @ edit.PEditItemsHandle(...)
> edit-items-saved

[edit-items-nochange] Added-items handler makes no plan changes <output>
= Newly added paths receive no Edit plan write from PEditItemsHandle.

[edit-restored] Edit state synchronized <output>
= Edit-specific crop/edit state reflects the viewer source/state that was current when PViewerMediaChange reached the Edit subscriber; that source can differ from the failure cargo's requested path.

[edit-items-saved] Added Edit plans synchronized <output>
= Carried Edit state has been resolved and saved for every newly added item.
